{{also|Fressen}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|frezzen}}, from {{inh|de|goh|frezzan}}, {{m|goh|firezzan}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*fraetaną}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|vreten}}, {{cog|da|fråse}}, {{cog|got|𐍆𐍂𐌰𐌹𐍄𐌰𐌽}}, {{cog|en|fret}}.

===Verb===
{{de-verb-strong|class=5|frisst|fraß|gefressen|past subjunctive=fräße}}

# {{lb|de|transitive|or|intransitive|of an animal}} to [[eat]]; to [[feed]] on; to [[devour]]
# {{lb|de|transitive|or|intransitive|of a person|pejorative}} to [[stuff]] oneself; to [[gorge]] oneself; to [[eat]] like a pig
# {{lb|de|figurative|chiefly|reflexive|_|with {{m|de|durch}}}} to [[eat away]] (e.g. metal)
# {{lb|de|figurative|transitive|}} to [[consume]], to [[guzzle]], to [[burn]] (e.g. fuel, money)
# {{lb|de|transitive|colloquial|perfect only}} to [[despise]], to have a [[pet peeve]] against
#: {{ux|de|Den hab ich ja '''gefressen!'''|I can’t stand that guy!|lit=I have eaten that one.|inline=1}}

